    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0053" n="39" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p1/pg39"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.6363/8–2348: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wadsworth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-23">August 23,
                        1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–241. Press reports that the Council of Ministers has approved of the formation
                    of a Ministerial Committee under the presidency of Prime Minister Muzahem
                    Pachachi with Finance Minister Ali Mumtaz al-Daftari and Economics Minister
                    Abdul Wahab Mirjan, as members, to study existing oil conventions, and contact
                    relative oil concessionaires for reconsideration of Iraq’s royalties.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d24-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wadsworth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d24-f1" n="1" xml:id="d24-f1-content">
                <p>The Minister of Economics, on October 19, addressed notes to the Iraq Petroleum
                    Company, the Mosul Petroleum Company, and the Basra Petroleum Company which
                    requested reconsideration of the terms of their oil concessions. The notes asked
                    for increased royalties, Iraqi participation in their capital structure and
                    management, computation of royalties on the basis of free market quotations for
                    gold, training of Iraqis to replace foreign personnel, and an increase in the
                    volume of oil exports (despatch 210, November 8, from Baghdad, and despatch 417,
                    November 15, from Lisbon, 890G.6363/11–848,/11–1548).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
